# Plaud cloud pipeline — nightly run.
# Install with `crontab -e` and adjust the path to where you cloned the repo.
#
# Runs at 03:00 every day (host local time — set the VM timezone, or use UTC and
# pick an off-peak hour). cron captures stdout/stderr; on a GCP VM the Ops Agent
# ships those to Cloud Logging, where a log-based alert watches for
# "[ALERT][PLAUD_AUTH_FAILED]" (see cloud/SETUP.md).
#
# The trailing logger line tags output so it is easy to find in journald.

0 3 * * * /path/to/free-plaud/cloud/run.sh 2>&1 | /usr/bin/logger -t plaud-pipeline
